## Common Mistakes

1. **Deserializing untrusted data** — Using Java ObjectInputStream, Python pickle, or PHP unserialize on user-controlled data. Deserialization of untrusted data is inherently dangerous.

2. **Shell command construction** — Building OS commands with string concatenation instead of using array-based execution (execFile vs exec, ProcessBuilder with argument lists vs single string).

3. **Eval on user input** — Using eval(), Function(), setTimeout(string), or equivalent dynamic code execution with any user-controlled data, even "sanitized" input.

4. **Missing input type enforcement** — Accepting raw objects where primitives are expected, enabling prototype pollution or type confusion attacks that lead to code execution.

## Secure Implementation

### Tier 1: Critical Fix (5 minutes)

**Use @RequestBody with Jackson/Gson instead of automatic POJO binding**

```java
// SECURE: Explicit JSON deserialization prevents property traversal
package com.example.userprofile.secure;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonProperty;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/profile")
public class SecureUserProfileController {

    @PostMapping("/update")
    public ResponseEntity<?> updateProfile(@RequestBody SecureUserProfile user) {
        // ✅ SECURE: JSON parsing only deserializes defined fields
        // No property traversal possible - Jackson only creates User object
        // Cannot access class.* properties

        System.out.println("User updated: " + user.getName());
        return ResponseEntity.ok("Profile updated successfully");
    }
}

// SECURE POJO: No spring parameter binding exposure
public class SecureUserProfile {
    @JsonProperty("name")
    private String name;

    @JsonProperty("email")
    private String email;

    @JsonProperty("bio")
    private String bio;

    // Constructor
    public SecureUserProfile() {}

    // Getters/Setters - only defined fields are accessible
    public String getName() { return name; }
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }

    public String getEmail() { return email; }
    public void setEmail(String email) { this.email = email; }

    public String getBio() { return bio; }
    public void setBio(String bio) { this.bio = bio; }
}

// SECURE: Use DTO pattern to limit exposed properties
public class UserProfileUpdateRequest {
    private String name;
    private String email;
    private String bio;

    // Only these 3 fields are deserialized, no class.* access possible

    public UserProfileUpdateRequest() {}
    public UserProfileUpdateRequest(String name, String email, String bio) {
        this.name = name;
        this.email = email;
        this.bio = bio;
    }

    public String getName() { return name; }
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }

    public String getEmail() { return email; }
    public void setEmail(String email) { this.email = email; }

    public String getBio() { return bio; }
    public void setBio(String bio) { this.bio = bio; }
}
```

